索 (cord/search), and the Korean syllable 소. Compounds such as 酵素 and
検索 have weaker responses. Incomplete UTF-8 tokens are treated separately:
starting a silk-character byte prefix is not the same event as finishing it.
Most other tokens, including most complete silk-radical characters, get zero.
Amplitudes are moderated because these rules omit contextual variation.
