A detached 5 is especially positive in familiar technical names (MD5,
HTML5, HDF5, Qt5, Perl5). Split endings of five/fifteen are also positive.
Ordinary digits have small biases. At document openings, whitespace tends
positive and unspaced words negative; two opening sequences are exceptional.
File-opening comment/docstring markers get their own rules. These are
coarse rules, not a reconstruction of arbitrary word responses. Other
positions default to zero. State is just a within-document token count
and the last 24 characters; both reset when the document changes.
