Strong negative outputs mark 'come up (with)', 'think of', and related phrases
about knowing, discovering, or recalling information. WordNet supplies verb
inflections. Separable phrases such as 'look it up' are included. Independent
spelling rules recognize mab/mod fragments across token boundaries, and runs
of middle dots. Other positions return zero; history resets at each document.
This approximates the large lexical responses, not every subword response.
